<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47813" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tĕnus</span></b> , ŏris,
			n.
		root ten-; Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τείνω;</span> v.
		teneo, = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τένος,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a cord</i>, <i>snare</i>, <i>gin</i>, <i>springe</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">intendere tenus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Bacch. 4, 6, 23</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tenus est laqueus, dictus a
					tendiculā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Non. 6, 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tenus est proprie extrema pars arcūs,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Serv. Verg. A. 6, 62</span></i>
			.</div>
